{
  "name": "tree-frog",
  "_about": "SCULPTED (2026-11-21, tools/creaturegen/rework/herps/treefrog.py): the EUROPEAN TREE FROG, Hyla arborea, 4.5 cm snout to vent, sitting. SLIM and smooth (no ridges, no warts), the skin glossy (wet); a short ROUND head with a blunt snout, BIG gold eyes set well out to the sides (a horizontal pupil), a small eardrum; LONG thin legs folded tight in a Z against the body, long fingers and toes each ending in a round STICKY DISC (pale pads), hardly any web; leaf-green above, a cream belly, and the DARK SIDE STRIPE (paints) from the nostril through the eye and over the eardrum along the flank to the groin, edged pale above, hooking UP into a loop at the hip. The common frog's rig and hop. Coats: green, brown phase, American green tree frog (Hyla cinerea: the stripe cream-white, x1.1).",
